      "associationCertaintyURI": "https://pleiades.stoa.org/vocabularies/association-certainty/certain",
      "start": 1500,
      "details": "<p class=\"p1\">Na\u1e2b\u015feb:\u00a0It is the city in <em data-start=\"32\" data-end=\"49\">M\u0101ver\u0101\u02be\u00fc\u2019n-Nehr</em> that they call <em data-start=\"65\" data-end=\"72\">Nesef</em>. There is a well there in which a moon can be seen. They say it is charming, and they call it the Well of Nakhshab (<em data-start=\"212\" data-end=\"226\">\u00c7\u0101h-\u0131 Na\u1e2b\u015feb</em>). (Translated to English by the first creator of this entry.)</p>",
      "review_state": "published",
      "description": "",
      "transcriptionCompleteness": "complete",
      "language": "ota",
      "created": "2025-11-08T01:02:03Z",
      "uri": "https://pleiades.stoa.org/places/60105/nahseb",
